
Usage: /PIPE <username> <command>
  Send  the output from the execution of <command> to <username>.  The
  <command>  is  executed in your environment, with your access level,
  etc.   Note  that  some door commands can not be piped because their
  executions are carried out by your MTalk client process, and not the
  server process.

  Example:
     /PIPE john /help

